the pool. She wanted to race, too.
She was about to dive. Beth knew
that Jill could not swim.
"Jill, don't dive!" Beth yelled.
Jill stopped. Their mother ran to ,
Jill and picked her up.
"Oh, thank you, Beth," her
mother said. "I watched you. I
didn't watch Jill. I'm sorry you
didn't get to race."
"That's all right," Beth said.
"Jill is safe. I'll try next time."

